# Normalise every text file to LF, in the index AND in the working tree.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate rather than plain `text=auto`. dist/ is committed build
# output (see .gitignore), and `scripts/copy-builtin-resources.js` copies YAML
# and JSON straight from lib/ into it. On a CRLF working tree those copies land
# in dist/ with CRLF, so the build stops being reproducible and CI's dist-fresh
# job fails on 80 files whose every line "changed". Forcing LF on checkout keeps
# a Windows build byte-identical to a Linux one.
#
# It also keeps Prettier (endOfLine: lf) honest on Windows checkouts, and the
# shell hooks in hooks/ valid — a CRLF shebang line is not executable.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
